      "message": "Don\u0027t use non-const reference args.  Pass a non-const pointer or return by value instead.\n\nThe bad thing about non-const reference args it that it\u0027s unclear at the call site that the function will modify the argument.\n\nhttps://engdoc.corp.google.com/eng/doc/devguide/cpp/styleguide.md?cl\u003dhead#Output_Parameters",
